## Why This Is Asked

This question tests mastery of rope-like data structures for dynamic sequences with cut-paste operations while maintaining fast range queries.

## Key Concepts

- **Implicit treap / rope**: Uses position as the key rather than explicit values
- **Split and merge operations**: Fundamental primitives for manipulating segments
- **Augmented data**: size and range sum maintained at each node
- **Edge cases**: Properly handling when dest overlaps with [l, r]

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(v) {
    this.v = v;
    this.pr = Math.random();
    this.l = this.r = null;
    this.sz = 1;
    this.sum = v;
  }
}

function upd(t) {
  if (!t) return;
  t.sz = 1 + sz(t.l) + sz(t.r);
  t.sum = t.v + sum(t.l) + sum(t.r);
}

function split(t, k, l, r) {
  if (!t) return [null, null];
  if (sz(t.l) >= k) {
    let [a, b] = split(t.l, k, l, r);
    t.l = b; upd(t);
    return [a, t];
  } else {
    let [a, b] = split(t.r, k - sz(t.l) - 1, l, r);
    t.r = a; upd(t);
    return [t, b];
  }
}

function merge(a, b) {
  if (!a || !b) return a || b;
  if (a.pr < b.pr) {
    a.r = merge(a.r, b); upd(a); return a;
  } else {
    b.l = merge(a, b.l); upd(b); return b;
  }
}

function rangeSum(t, l, r) {
  let [a, bc] = split(t, l);
  let [b, c] = split(bc, r - l + 1);
  let res = sum(b);
  t = merge(a, merge(b, c));
  return res;
}

function moveSegment(t, l, r, dest) {
  let len = r - l + 1;
  let [a, bc] = split(t, l);
  let [b, c] = split(bc, len);
  t = merge(a, c);

  let pos = dest <= l ? dest : dest - len;
  let [x, y] = split(t, pos);\n  return merge(merge(x, b), y);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of dynamic order-statistics with duplicates and memory efficiency without full value-domain indexing.

## Key Concepts

- Coordinate compression
- Fenwick Tree or Segment Tree for counts
- K-th element via prefix-sum search
- Handling duplicates through counts

## Code Example

```javascript
class Fenwick {
  constructor(n){ this.n=n; this.ft=Array(n+1).fill(0); }
  add(i,delta){ for(; i<=this.n; i+= i & -i) this.ft[i]+=delta; }
  sum(i){ let s=0; for(; i>0; i-= i & -i) s+= this.ft[i]; return s; }
  kth(k){ let idx=0; let bit=1; while(bit<<1 <= this.n) bit<<=1; for(let d=bit; d; d>>=1){ let next=idx+d; if(next<=this.n && this.ft[next] < k){ idx = next; k -= this.ft[next]; } } return idx+1; }
}
```

